Well, I can't see any new aspects even from that angle. Though, from my
perspective, I even have to disagree. Presuming I count as an advanced
player, my "WoW usage history" was like that; a couple years ago I had
often saved the available wishes and finished the game wishless, or at
least with a lot of wishes left, later I used those wishes for various
non-"standard AK" items, often just for conveniences.

> More wish variation is IMO a "Good Thing"[tm].

Certainly. I think for non-advanced players it's harder to wish for
non-AK items. People will and have to learn where they get the necessary
items with highest probability and how to adjust their play according
the goal without wishing up for everything.

>> [wand wresting]
> 
