Yes, it is. And if the feature-set (0 charges / 121 wrests) is in the
reach of influence to change that to something less tedious, change it
to something less tedious. Since it's a parameter tuple (1/121) there
are at least two apparent changes; (1/121) or (0/11), for example.

>>> There are just way too many wishing sources in vanilla.
>> Most are just unreliable faint chances (thrones, fountains), and the
> 
> For fountains I'd call it a small chance, not a faint.

Well, we can call it as we like, since faint/small are vague attributes
anyway. The problem with fountains is that they have bad side effects;
you should at least take that into account in your considerations. But,
yes, I consider also the small chance of wishes with random fountains
as no good rationale for a 0/121 feature. If you think fountains (with
all their inherent risks) are broken WRT wishes, then just remove that
part of the fountain feature. (Just to make it clear; I wouldn't think
that fountain wishes should be changed.)

> There are some obsessive fountain quaffers out there and I've
> witnessed many wishes early in the game from fountains.

What's the survival rate of those people? (Just go and calculate the
probabilities for such fountains in the upper 20 dungeon levels, and
the probabilities for wishes from fountains, and those for the bad
fountains effects, then estimate for the average player whether that's
the best way to survive. Also take into account that you need a low
dungeon level fountain to get the best probabilities and to survive
best you should be an advanced character, so that [in extreme] you
would be ready for the Castle to turn back to level I and start the
fountain dipping.) My survival rate increased when I stopped fiddling
with fountains (especially very early in the game).

